  "narrative": {
    "intro": "DDB Chicago obligated $303M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. DDB Chicago won 11 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $27.6M. Obligations are down 22.4% year over year. Yearly obligations for DDB Chicago show $348M in FY21, $363M in FY22, $596M in FY23, $399M in FY24, $391M in FY25, and $303M in FY26. The FY26 total is a partial fiscal-year to date figure and represents the latest point in a multi-year sequence that peaked at $596M in FY23. The average award size and the small count of awards imply a concentration in larger contract actions rather than many small purchases. The year-over-year decline of down 22.4% signals lower near-term obligations compared with the prior fiscal period. Readers should regard the FY26 totals as incomplete for the full fiscal year, while the historical series provides a clear record of changing obligation levels across FY21 through FY26.",
